From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:11:12 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] UNFILED 89: the rotated constraint-row diagonal scale is
 bit-identical run to run

_velocity_diag_scale, the mean |diag| of the rotated velocity block, is written
on the eliminated wall-normal rows (forward and adjoint) and scales the
rotation gauge test. It was NORM_1 of a getSubVector, which is BLAS dasum. On
AVX-512 OpenBLAS, dasum of the same data gives one of two results an ulp
apart, depending on the array's alignment: 89 of 90 random vectors differ by
offset, while NORM_2, dot, sum and NORM_INFINITY do not. getSubVector's array
lands somewhere new on each call. On H7's warm re-solve fixture (annulus,
viscosity 1 + T) the ulp moved Krylov round-off, and the pressure sub-solve
took 12, 13 or its 200 cap from run to run at np 2, with the same answer.

Each rank now sums with math.fsum (exactly rounded), and the ranks' sums are
gathered and summed the same way: bit-identical every run at a given rank
count. No other NORM_1 in src.

Test first: test_1089 (50 calls must return the reference bits) fails serially
on development and passes at np 1, 2 and 3. The fixture at np 2, 10 runs:
development 13 x8 and 200 x2; this branch 13 x10, one operator hash.

